  "id": "lateral-lemniscus",
  "term": "lateral lemniscus",
  "definition": "The lateral lemniscus is an auditory brainstem pathway that includes nuclei such as the ventral nucleus of the lateral lemniscus (VNLL). In the source, cells in this system respond to sound with very fast inhibition that can reduce broadband onset noise and sharpen the representation of harmonic sound content.",
